are called out separately from fixture outputs; unresolved closure is explicit.

001  narrow-literal-proofs
Producer: bin/prepare-narrow-literal-proofs.py:main
Consumers: thc.runtime.NarrowLiteralProofTest; producer --check-only.
The deleted test-narrow-literal-proofs.py is not a current consumer.

Apparent direct inputs:
  t/fixtures/compiler/NarrowLiteralProofAudit.hs
  t/fixtures/compiler/NarrowLiteralProofAuditNative.hs (imports the first module)
  bin/prepare-narrow-literal-proofs.py (generation, projections and checked model)
  bin/build-compiler.sh, bin/export-core.sh, bin/toolchain.sh, bin/plugin.py
  bin/core_package_manifest.py and bin/core_original_foreign.py (CBD inspection)
  bin/audit-core.py and its imported core_* modules
  bin/core-capabilities.json
  src/main/resources/thc/scalar-primop-signatures.json
  src/test/resources/thc/polyglot-abi.json (audit-core import-time read)
  bin/simd-families.json (core_vectors import-time read)
  Tools: selected GHC 9.14.1, matching ghc-pkg, Cabal, Python, shell;
    THC Core plugin/shared library and package registration; thc-compact executable.
  Native Haskell inputs include GHC.Exts and its selected compiler package closure.
  The plugin/tool build reads thc.cabal, cabal.project, Setup.hs, relevant Haskell
    component sources and Cabal's resolved plan/package databases. That shared
    build closure is not yet individually enumerated here.

Selection/configuration consumed:
  GHC, GHC_PKG, CABAL, THC_COMPACT; PATH for unresolved tool names.
  THC_SOURCE_NOTES defaults to true in export-core.sh.
  GHC_ENVIRONMENT and Cabal configuration are inherited, not cleared by this script.
  Producer supplies THC_CORE_OUT and THC_GHC_OUT per stage.
  Export flags: -O2 -dynamic -fforce-recomp -dcore-lint; post stage adds post-tidy.
  Native flags: --make -O2 -fforce-recomp; target platform/word size/native ABI apply.

Published outputs, relative to build/narrow-literal-proofs/:
  pre-core/NarrowLiteralProofAudit.cbd
  post-core/NarrowLiteralProofAudit.cbd
  pre-audit.json, post-audit.json
  oracle.tsv
  native/narrow-literal-oracle
  manifest.json (sources/artifacts with hashes, commands and model inventory)
Intermediate outputs:
  pre-ghc/, post-ghc/, native/ object/interface files; compiler/plugin publication;
  Cabal build products; temporary CBD inspection files. Exporter may emit further
  diagnostic products: inspect the exporter/plugin closure before declaring these.

Actual test reads:
  manifest.json; every path in its sources and artifacts sections;
  pre/post CBD and oracle.tsv. Native executable/audit files are also read as bytes
  by manifest verification, even when the test does not execute/read their contents.
  Runtime/test classpath and test implementation are separate test inputs.

Artifact-by-artifact file flow (paths below use this fixture directory):
  native/narrow-literal-oracle
    IN: NarrowLiteralProofAuditNative.hs, NarrowLiteralProofAudit.hs, selected
        GHC package interfaces/libraries and native linker/compiler tools.
    OUT: native/narrow-literal-oracle; native object/interface intermediates.
  pre-core/NarrowLiteralProofAudit.cbd
    IN: NarrowLiteralProofAudit.hs, published THC plugin/package DB, GHC package
        interfaces, export-core.sh/toolchain.sh/plugin.py and export flags.
    OUT: that CBD; pre-ghc/ intermediates. Further plugin side outputs unresolved.
  post-core/NarrowLiteralProofAudit.cbd
    IN: same as pre, plus the post-tidy plugin option.
    OUT: that CBD; post-ghc/ intermediates. Further plugin side outputs unresolved.
  oracle.tsv
    IN: native/narrow-literal-oracle (executed with its embedded input cases).
    OUT: captured stdout as oracle.tsv.
  pre-audit.json / post-audit.json (two separate files)
    IN: the corresponding stage CBD, oracle.tsv, checked model in the producer,
        thc-compact, auditor Python import closure and JSON tables listed above.
    OUT: corresponding audit JSON; temporary decoded Core JSON is not published.
  manifest.json
    IN: all six artifact files above (both CBDs, both audits, oracle TSV and
        native executable); the exact source paths assembled in main(); commands.
    OUT: manifest.json. This happens after all generation/checks succeed.

Missing edges / caveats:
  The producer builds the plugin itself, and each export builds it again. Those are
  procedural calls rather than shared producer edges.
  Decoder availability is reached indirectly through build-compiler.sh, which
  currently builds exe:thc-compact; inspection otherwise only locates the executable.
  The fixture's source receipt omits bin/plugin.py and polyglot-abi.json despite
  consuming them; bin/simd-families.json is also an imported data input. Its src/compiler/THC/**/*.hs and core_*.py lists also hash files
  more broadly than their proven consumption.
  --check-only rewrites pre/post audit JSON; it is not a read-only verification step.
  Current Gradle input globs do not create a producer dependency. The former Python
  test exposed this by reading oracle.tsv before any producer had run.

