  environment. Options --export-only and --ghc-option affect outputs/content.
  Current manifest wrapper uses uname -m: ARM gets export-only (pre stage, no
  native oracle); other hosts get pre/post plus native. Extra GHC options default
  empty; no automatic LLVM flag in the default non-ARM branch.

  For each family, before generation the function READS existing provenance.json
  and every prior artifacts[].path and COPIES them into a fresh random
  prepare-run-*/previous/ tree. A missing old file fails even if a clean rebuild
  could produce it. This is an actual backward dependency on previous outputs,
  and accumulating archival state; candidate for deletion under current user policy.
  Fresh attempt directories are also embedded in the newly produced receipt, so
  successful output is not determined solely by source/toolchain content.

  Common artifact flow under that family's build directory:
    expected.tsv: IN model rows/expected functions; OUT independently modeled TSV.
    requests.tsv: IN same case inventory; OUT native stdin without expected results.
    <stage>-core/<module>.cbd
      IN: tracked fixture source, plugin/exporter, ghcOptions/stage/export-only flags.
      OUT: CBD; <stage>-ghc/ intermediates. Stage CBD is deleted before export.
    prepare-run-*/audits/<stage>-<entry>.json
      IN: stage CBD, entry, capabilities, auditor/decoder/data.
      OUT: accepted reports for entries/graphNames/hostEntries, rejected report
        for readTupleEscape. Entry families come from SimdByteArrayModel.hs.
    prepare-run-*/mutations/<stage>-wrong-<element>-<offset><op>.cbd
      IN: stage CBD and producer mutation code, in-process Haskell CBD writer.
      OUT: mutated proof CBD; offset=vector/scalar, op=Index/Read/Write.
    prepare-run-*/audits/<same mutation label>.json
      IN: mutation CBD, auditor/decoder/data; OUT negative audit report.
    pre-audit.json and post-audit.json (enabled stages only)
      IN: in-memory stage entry reports; OUT combined JSON report.
    native/<family>-oracle (native mode only)
      IN: tracked <module>Native.hs and imported <module>.hs, GHC/packages,
          ghcOptions; OUT executable and native/ .hi/.o files.
    oracle.tsv (native only)
      IN: executable, requests.tsv, byte comparison with model; OUT native TSV.
    prepare-run-*/commands/<label>.{stdout,stderr,command.json}
      Labels ghc-version, ghc-info, host, architecture, system, compiler-build,
        each stage-export/entry/mutation audit; native-build/native-oracle if enabled.
      IN: commands and their inputs; OUT three log files per command.
    provenance.json and prepare-run-*/provenance.json
      IN: source records, all fresh artifacts/logs, stage report data, host/options;
      OUT: two copies of current receipt.

  Source receipt additionally hashes Java VectorMemoryFamily.java, VectorMemoryOp.java,
  VectorReadCase.java, CoreVectorMemory.java, VectorByteArrayExpression.java (all in
  src/main/java/thc/runtime), although fixture generation does not execute JVM code.
  Double family also hashes VectorMemory.java. This ties regeneration to runtime
  changes without a producer computation that consumes those implementations.
  Receipt omits imported polyglot ABI and SIMD JSON tables. Top-level-only compiler
  receipt caveat remains. Native filenames have no explicit .exe suffix branch.
  Tests read receipt source/artifact bytes, selected stage CBDs, expected/oracle TSV;
  SimdByteArrayEvidence reads command records; SimdByteArrayCorpus reads expected/
  oracle TSV. Their local helper file reads are included; no subprocess in Java.

