Shared installed fixture artifact flow (read once for later entries)
Owner: t/haskell-fixtures/InstalledCoreFixtures.hs:prepareInstalledCoreProfile.
IN: selected GHC/GHC_PKG/CABAL; built thc-fixtures and production Driver modules;
  thc.cabal/Cabal package closure; dist-newstyle/cache/plan.json; installed package
  registrations, their transitive interfaces/native libraries; target-layout.c.
  Optional THC_INSTALLED_CORE_GHC and THC_INSTALLED_CORE_GHC_PKG select a complete
  Core provider; THC_INSTALLED_CORE_GHC_SOURCE or explicit source selects foreign
  annotation rebuild. THC_CACHE_HOME selects shared cache location.
Artifacts relative to caller's fixture directory:
  logs/helper-build.*: Cabal builds exe:thc and exe:thc-interface (shared dist-newstyle).
  logs/helper-location.*, driver-location.*: discover the two executables.
  installed/staging/: Project.prepareInstalledBundle uses selected interfaces/
    native libraries and src/driver/cbits/target-layout.c to produce/validate bundle.
  Shared cache: IN interface/compiler/native identity; OUT production bundles;
    missing retained Core invokes Wired.preparePinnedInterfaces, which additionally
    reads build/compiler/plugin.json and its packageDb/unitId/sharedLibrary.
    Foreign profile additionally consumes supplied compiler source, registered
    Cabal library and driver executable hash. Exact provider/cache files unresolved
    until shared production driver scan; do not infer a complete dependency closure.
  installed/bundles/<unit-id>.zip: IN corresponding verified cache bundle;
    OUT fixture-local copy after hash comparison.
  installed/unit-core/v3/<bundle-hash>/: IN copied bundle/Driver.CoreSymbols;
    OUT per-module CBD files and publication.json, named by returned package records.
  installed/packages.json: IN all published unit records/dependency closure;
    OUT format thc-core-packages, schema 1.
Returned artifacts exclude staging/helper binaries and include package manifest,
  ZIPs, published CBDs/publications. Caller hashes these; command logs include
  version, helper build/locations, provider version if set, package registrations.
This helper assumes compiler/plugin.json already exists when fallback is needed;
  the helper's Cabal build does not publish it. Make that producer dependency explicit.

